Subject: [PATCH 3/7] docs(adr): record the bounded verdict re-read as a
 publish-gate relay assumption (review 5260334866)

Root AGENTS.md requires a new relay assumption to be explicit in documentation
("No new event kinds, payment semantics, relay assumptions, or network egress
paths without code, tests, and documentation that make the decision explicit").
ADR-0004 owns publish-layer quorum-gate semantics, so the assumption lands
there as an amendment on the settlement publisher section: the bounded window
and step, that only an empty read or a transient transport error is re-read,
that an auditor-less auction is not retried, and that the re-read cannot weaken
the fail-closed gate.

Proposed, not accepted: the amendment says so in place and the ADR Status field
is unchanged, because the decision awaits maintainer sign-off (PR #1380,
maxime-tt review 5260334866, "Required before merge" item 2).

Prettier-clean: `bunx prettier --check` on the touched files passes.
