Review 5320097003 (maxime-tt), item 5, verbatim: "the new test's header
comment (src/queries/__tests__/auctionVerdictsRetry.test.ts:21-25)
overstates its independence from the process-wide mock.module registry."

Comment-only. The old text implied this file's mocks were the seam and that
"staying identical to auctionVerdicts.test.ts" was enough. It is not: bun
applies `mock.module` process-wide for the whole `bun run test:unit` run, so
this file registers its mocks but does not control the registry another
co-running file populates. The corrected comment says what the file does
control — its own really-signed fixtures, so the deliberately unmocked
signature seam behaves as in production — and what it does not.
